[36m(TaskRunner pid=2544157)[0m [response] Let $z = 4e^{i\theta}$. Then, the given expression becomes
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2544157)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2544157)[0m (75+117i)z+\frac{96+144i}{z} &= (75+117i)4e^{i\theta}+\frac{96+144i}{4e^{i\theta}} \\
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2544157)[0m &= 300e^{i\theta}+468ie^{i\theta}+24e^{-i\theta}+36ie^{-i\theta} \\
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2544157)[0m &= (300+24\cos\theta+36\sin\theta)e^{i\theta}+(468\sin\theta-36\cos\theta)e^{i\theta} \\
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2544157)[0m &= (324+24\cos\theta+36\sin\theta)e^{i\theta}+(468\sin\theta-36\cos\theta)e^{i\theta} \\
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2544157)[0m &= (324+492\sin\theta)e^{i\theta} \\
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2544157)[0m &= 324e^{i\theta}+492e^{i\theta}\sin\theta.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2544157)[0m \end{align*}The real part of this expression is $324\cos\theta+492\sin\theta\cos\theta$. We want to maximize this expression. We can rewrite it as
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2544157)[0m \[324\cos\theta+492\sin\theta\cos\theta = 324\cos\theta+246\sin2\theta.\]By the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we have
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2544157)[0m \[(324^2+246^2)(\cos^2\theta+\sin^22\theta) \ge (324\cos\theta+246\sin2\theta)^2,\]so
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2544157)[0m \[324^2+246^2 \ge (324\cos\theta+246\sin2\theta)^2.\]Therefore, the maximum value of $324\cos\theta+246\sin2\theta$ is $\sqrt{324^2+246^2} = 408$. This maximum value is achieved when $\cos\theta = \frac{324}{408} = \frac{9}{10}$ and $\sin2\theta = \frac{246}{408} = \frac{41}{81}$. Therefore, the largest possible real part of the given expression is $\boxed{408}$.
